#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096427 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "12811582-7156-5b84-9ba9-5545f87894f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-3993" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "c7373a16-c90a-5875-8b17-8724542b35ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-493" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096476 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "672d52f6-89d8-550d-863b-7c5157d59ca3" :question/math-academy-id "e-494" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d0d172-5a30-57d5-a766-d99669bdec9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257411} {:answer/id #uuid "5650ea15-d618-5b47-8c28-c84f1b05c79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257525} {:answer/id #uuid "b25a9222-222c-5e15-ba09-a0c57522e510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258336} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b91501-5eb2-51d9-8768-15ceeaa9babf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258785} {:answer/id #uuid "eec4b01f-b497-53f1-8b34-4b8b2d67f6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec4b01f-b497-53f1-8b34-4b8b2d67f6ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258851} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b1e6c3d-3d86-5dab-9cbb-0d0320668747" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8f0b656-4bc9-55ad-bafd-83e444f61957" :question/math-academy-id "q-12568" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(3x)\\cdot (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(3x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c987d6e-0dd9-50fa-85a0-905c93e07413" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing an Arbitrary Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0155e70c-7153-50ac-ae32-b2c98bd947de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256794} {:answer/id #uuid "492b97f9-d3ef-59ab-b561-3b0dcf2167b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257422} {:answer/id #uuid "528a8324-2d4a-5fa6-b598-f741cb33ee5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257489} {:answer/id #uuid "57f151a3-62b4-585a-a72e-e79e50e78a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257543} {:answer/id #uuid "eff5e611-dfe2-5583-8b84-0312c0fe1b79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57f151a3-62b4-585a-a72e-e79e50e78a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257543} :answer-field/id #uuid "f07a98a3-4e03-5c25-9500-65acccf243a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ce071f41-118b-504d-a520-d6c46fbbaaf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-12570" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e^5+1}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2596bc-8831-5738-bc87-23664928dc31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e^5+1}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424983} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0c4dfe-2a2c-535e-956d-62ad8cee8229" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48a4330e-b61a-5908-b482-77c947469ce8" :question/math-academy-id "q-350842" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\,dx=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{1}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{5}]-\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{5}}{5}-(\\frac{{e}^{5}}{25}-\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(5{e}^{5}-{e}^{5}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}(4{e}^{5}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31a28451-005e-50dc-a7cf-5b666b1d7735" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "207a1d95-c0ea-56d4-a5bc-ef262d85c6e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319492} {:answer/id #uuid "e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e33bd3cc-1587-505f-a1f3-81e0ab86915b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17e^{18}+1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424989} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0007b9-ddd0-5502-af59-9a118bd8d4d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a9908cce-81d8-5c41-be9b-94f0b6365826" :question/math-academy-id "q-350960" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{5} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{5}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{3})^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{18}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{18}-(\\frac{{e}^{18}}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(18{e}^{18}-{e}^{18}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a39296-35ee-53cf-bfb8-6a10b78a1084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330379} {:answer/id #uuid "54c780ec-8ed0-59df-9662-49d663639bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330714} {:answer/id #uuid "d22501a3-a221-5893-92d1-782b53f97c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331815} {:answer/id #uuid "ee61e062-2a60-5418-91a5-bc857edab7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332044} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9ebae5-f2cd-530f-bdd8-1769730a7359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54c780ec-8ed0-59df-9662-49d663639bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330714} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba7992fb-af57-5bce-a970-c192ca7e1d84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a51e949-edb8-581f-9b0d-82187677b8f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-49712" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(x){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e-x{|}_{1}^{e}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}(e-e+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4435e346-d6ad-58cd-97cb-bbd45e121759" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Integral Containing a Single Logarithmic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fac7b1b-401e-571f-9ac1-c8035cba4079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424984} {:answer/id #uuid "612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424985} {:answer/id #uuid "92b952c7-daa6-5ab4-a7f5-81b3cf909d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424986} {:answer/id #uuid "bd63e3cd-ff82-5ade-9211-594e2bfdb08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424987} {:answer/id #uuid "cc74e90b-cf7b-5156-89e6-293ad43d67ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "612aede7-2fcb-5f05-9a9e-41d69e0a1e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424985} :answer-field/id #uuid "8afc707b-a42b-5621-ace9-e6a014a201bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45517c4f-34c5-5613-91b3-714b64a55e54" :question/math-academy-id "q-78972" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant."}]}
